# Local configuration for scripts/anonymize.py — copy to `.env.anonymize`
# and fill in with the mailbox owner's real identity. `.env.anonymize` is
# gitignored; this `.example` file is committed and must never contain real
# personal data.
#
# These values are the ONE identity the pipeline redacts. Everything else in
# the corpus (sender domains, IPs, third-party addresses) is deliberately
# left real — see the "Gizlilik/anonimleştirme" decision in CLAUDE.md.

# The mailbox owner's own email address. Redacted as a literal substring,
# including URL-encoded and double-encoded occurrences inside tracking links.
ANONYMIZE_OWN_EMAIL="you@example.com"

# The mailbox owner's own name, in known variants, pipe-separated.
# Whitespace inside a variant is matched flexibly (one or more spaces).
#
# Do NOT list a bare surname on its own: surnames are shared with unrelated
# third parties, and matching one alone would redact a different real
# person's name as if it were the mailbox owner's. List the first name and
# multi-word combinations that include it.
ANONYMIZE_OWN_NAME_VARIANTS="Firstname Lastname|Firstname|Nickname Lastname"
